 "text": "The man famous for finding Troy may have destroyed the real Troy. For centuries, people think the Trojan War is just a myth from Homer. Then a British official, Frank Calvert, becomes convinced Troy lies under a hill in Turkey called Hisarlik. In 1870, a rich German businessman, Heinrich Schliemann, arrives, on Calvert's advice. He cuts a giant trench straight through the hill, tossing away layers he thinks are too young. In 1873, he announces Priam's Treasure, gold of Troy's legendary king. But it's from a layer about 1,000 years older than Homer's Troy, and he smuggles it out of the country. A legend found, and nearly ruined, by its hunter. Every legend has a beginning.",
